														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4122163">
									

<p>While the first usage could be Keter, that would come at the cost of losing the impact of the third object class (Keter-Neutralised-Keter) doesn't have the same punch. Also, on a meta level, if Archon is something that we explicitly shouldn't restrict, lest we face dire consequences, then our biosphere and natural habitats are real life Archon entities. (If I'm allowed to be a preachy environmentalist.)</p>
<p>The final usage however explicitly can't be Thaumiel. The Thaumiel class, by definition, is used for anomalies that are used to answer other anomalies. And Gaia mostly exists in isolation.</p>

							</div>

								
					
